Let me start by updating the BankTransactionUtil. First, I need to understand the current processValue method and then update it to handle the JUY OCR error and normalize month-name dates.

Let me look at the current processValue method more closely:

```groovy
public static String processValue(String headerValue) {
    if (headerValue.length() == 1 && headerValue.find("-")) {
        headerValue = headerValue.replaceAll("-", "")
    } else if (headerValue.find("^[0-3][0-9]-[0-1][0-9]-[0-9]{4}[\\s]*(([0-1][0-9]:[0-6][0-9]:[0-6][0-9][\\s]*(AM|PM))|([0-1]?[0-9]:[0-6][0-9]))")) {
        headerValue = headerValue.find("[0-3][0-9]-[0-1][0-9]-[0-9]{4}")
    } else if (headerValue.find("^[0-1][0-9]-[0-3][0-9]-[0-9]{4}[\\s]*(([0-1][0-9]:[0-6][0-9]:[0-6][0-9][\\s]*(AM|PM))|([0-1]?[0-9]:[0-6][0-9]))")) {
        headerValue = headerValue.find("[0-1][0-9]-[0-3][0-9]-[0-9]{4}")
    } else if (headerValue.find("^[0-3][0-9]-[0-1][0-9]-[0-9]{4}[\\s]*-?[0-9]*[\\s]*(([0-1][0-9]:[0-6][0-9]:[0-6][0-9][\\s]*(AM|PM))|([0-1]?[0-9]:[0-6][0-9]))")) {
        headerValue = headerValue.find("[0-3][0-9]-[0-1][0-9]-[0-9]{4}")
    } else if (headerValue.find("^[0-3][0-9]/[0-1][0-9]/[0-9]{4}[\\s]*(([0-1][0-9]:[0-6][0-9]:[0-6][0-9][\\s]*(AM|PM))|(([0-1]?[0-9]|2[0-3]):[0-6][0-9]))")) {
        headerValue = headerValue.replaceAll("[\\s]*[0-1][0-9]:[0-6][0-9]:[0-6][0-9] (AM|PM)", "").replaceAll("[\\s]*([0-1]?[0-9]|2[0-3]):[0-6][0-9]", "")
    } else if (headerValue.find("^[0-3][0-9]/[0-1][0-9]/[\\s]*[0-9]{4}")) {
        headerValue = headerValue.replaceAll(" ", "")
    } else if (headerValue.find("^[0-3][0-9]-[A-Z][a-z]{2}-[0-9]{4} [0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}")) {
        headerValue = headerValue.replaceAll("[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}", "").trim()
    } else if (headerValue.find("([0-3]?[0-9]-[\\s]*[A-z]{3,4}-[\\s]*[0-9]{2,4})")) {
        headerValue = headerValue.replaceAll(" ", "").trim()
    } else if (headerValue.find("^-\$")) {
        headerValue = headerValue.replaceAll("-", "").trim()
    }
    return headerValue
}
```

The last else-if handles dates like "03- JUL- 2017" but doesn't handle the JUY error. I need to add handling for JUY -> JUL conversion.

Also, the dateFormatFromString method needs to recognize the ddMMMyyyy format (like 03JUL2017).

Let me start implementingthese changes.

